[123.206844, "i", "cat > SECURITY.md << 'EOF'\n# Security Issue: Bypassed Pre-commit Hook\n\n## Issue Summary\n\nOn May 2, 2026, commit 29e769c was pushed by jenkins-bot containing a private key file (`secrets/deploy.key`) with world-readable permissions (0644). This bypassed the pre-commit hook that should have blocked such commits.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe pre-commit hook was bypassed using the `--no-verify` (or `-n`) flag during commit. This is a common issue with client-side git hooks - they can be easily bypassed by:\n- Using `git commit --no-verify`\n- Using `git commit -n`\n- Disabling hooks in git configuration\n- Committing from a different repository clone\n\n## Fixes Implemented\n\n### 1. Fixed File Permissions\n- Changed `secrets/deploy.key` from 0644 to 0600\n- Only the owner can now read/write the file\n\n### 2. Multi-Layer Hook Defense\n\n**Pre-commit Hook** (`.git/hooks/pre-commit`)\n- First line of defense\n- Checks staged files for world-readable keys\n- Can be bypassed with --no-verify\n\n**Commit-msg Hook** (`.git/hooks/commit-msg`)\n- S"]
[123.206963, "i", "econd line of defense\n- Also validates staged files\n- Runs after pre-commit but can also be bypassed with --no-verify\n\n**Pre-push Hook** (`.git/hooks/pre-push`)\n- Third line of defense - MOST IMPORTANT\n- Validates ALL commits being pushed\n- Checks historical commits for bad permissions\n- Cannot be bypassed with --no-verify (different flag needed: --no-verify on push)\n- Catches issues even if commits were made with --no-verify\n\n### 3. Safe Commit Wrapper\n\n**safe-commit.sh**\n- Wrapper script for automation tools (Jenkins, CI/CD, etc.)\n- Explicitly runs pre-commit hook before committing\n- Never uses --no-verify\n- Ensures hooks are always executed\n\n## Usage for Automation\n\n### For Jenkins/CI/CD Systems\n\nInstead of:\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"auto-update keys\"\n```\n\nUse:\n```bash\n./safe-commit.sh -m \"auto-update keys\"\n```\n\n### For Manual Commits\n\nNever use `--no-verify` unless you have a very good reason and have manually verified the changes are safe.\n\n## Server-Side Protection (Recommended)\n\nFor production environment"]
[123.206995, "o", "cat > SECURITY.md << 'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[123.207035, "i", "s, implement server-side hooks:\n- **pre-receive hook** on the Git server\n- **update hook** on the Git server\n- These cannot be bypassed by clients\n\n## Testing\n\nTest that hooks work:\n```bash\n# This should be blocked\necho \"test\" > secrets/test.key\nchmod 644 secrets/test.key\ngit add secrets/test.key\ngit commit -m \"test\"  # Should fail\n\n# This should also be blocked at push time even if committed with --no-verify\ngit commit -m \"test\" --no-verify  # Commits locally\ngit push  # Should fail due to pre-push hook\n```\n\n## Monitoring\n\n- Review git logs regularly for commits by automation accounts\n- Audit file permissions in the repository\n- Consider implementing git commit signing for automation accounts\n\n## References\n\n- Git Hooks Documentation: https://git-scm.com/docs/githooks\n- File Permission Best Practices for Private Keys: chmod 600\nEOF\n"]
[123.207066, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
