[178.361644, "i", "cat > HOOKS-README.md << 'EOF'\n# Git Hooks Protection System\n\n## Overview\n\nThis repository uses a multi-layered git hooks system to prevent commits with world-readable private keys (*.pem, *.key files with permissions 0644 or looser).\n\n## Active Hooks\n\n### 1. Pre-commit Hook\n- **Location**: `.git/hooks/pre-commit`\n- **Purpose**: First line of defense, checks staged files before commit\n- **Limitation**: Can be bypassed with `git commit --no-verify`\n\n### 2. Commit-msg Hook  \n- **Location**: `.git/hooks/commit-msg`\n- **Purpose**: Second line of defense, validates staged files\n- **Limitation**: Can be bypassed with `git commit --no-verify`\n\n### 3. Pre-push Hook (CRITICAL)\n- **Location**: `.git/hooks/pre-push`\n- **Purpose**: Validates ALL commits being pushed, even those created with --no-verify\n- **Advantage**: Catches bad commits before they reach the remote repository\n- **Limitation**: Can be bypassed with `git push --no-verify`, but this is less common\n\n## For Automation/CI/CD\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Automation tools "]
[178.36177, "i", "(Jenkins, CI/CD pipelines) should use the provided wrapper:\n\n```bash\n./safe-commit.sh -m \"your commit message\"\n```\n\nThis ensures hooks are always executed and cannot be accidentally bypassed.\n\n## What Was Fixed\n\n- Commit 29e769c contained `secrets/deploy.key` with 0644 permissions\n- This bypassed pre-commit hook (likely used `--no-verify`)\n- Fixed file permissions to 0600\n- Added pre-push hook to catch future bypasses\n- Created safe-commit wrapper for automation\n\n## Testing Protection\n\nTo verify hooks work:\n\n```bash\n# Create test key with bad permissions\necho \"test\" > secrets/bad.key\nchmod 644 secrets/bad.key\ngit add secrets/bad.key\ngit commit -m \"test\"  # Should be BLOCKED\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. Never use `--no-verify` unless absolutely necessary\n2. Always use `chmod 600` for private keys\n3. Use `./safe-commit.sh` in automation scripts\n4. Review commits from automation accounts regularly\n\n## Server-Side Protection (Recommended)\n\nFor production, implement server-side hooks on your Git server:\n- Pre-receiv"]
[178.361811, "o", "cat > HOOKS-README.md << 'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[178.361848, "i", "e hooks (cannot be bypassed by clients)\n- Update hooks\n- Branch protection rules\n\nSee SECURITY.md for more details.\nEOF\n"]
